---
description: >-
  Every ER label kind written each way the grammar takes (#1368): entity
  name, alias, attribute cells, comment, relationship label and subgraph title.
  Only a markdown string "`…`" reads markdown; plain **bold** _ital_ and a code
  span are drawn as written; the tags draw; a written \n breaks a comment and a
  relationship label. Bare backticks parse in no ER label, and a \n is a parse
  error in a name, an alias or a subgraph title, as in v12.
---
erDiagram
  P1["alias **bold** _ital_"] {
    **type** _name_ "comment **bold** _ital_"
  }
  P2["`alias **bold** _ital_`"] {
    string mdString "`comment **bold** _ital_`"
  }
  P3["alias a `code` b"] {
    string codeSpan "comment a `code` b"
  }
  P4["alias <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>alias H<sub>2</sub>O"]
  P5 {
    string tags "comment <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>comment H<sub>2</sub>O"
    string newline "comment one\ntwo"
  }
  subgraph S1["subgraph **bold** _ital_"]
    "entity **bold** _ital_"
  end
  subgraph S2["`subgraph **bold** _ital_`"]
    "`entity **bold** _ital_`"
  end
  subgraph S3["subgraph a `code` b"]
    "entity a `code` b"
  end
  subgraph S4["subgraph <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>subgraph H<sub>2</sub>O"]
    "entity <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>entity H<sub>2</sub>O"
  end
  P1 ||--o{ "entity **bold** _ital_" : "relationship **bold** _ital_"
  P2 ||--o{ "`entity **bold** _ital_`" : "`relationship **bold** _ital_`"
  P3 ||--o{ "entity a `code` b" : "relationship a `code` b"
  P4 ||--o{ "entity <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>entity H<sub>2</sub>O" : "relationship <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>relationship H<sub>2</sub>O"
  P4 ||--o{ P5 : "relationship one\ntwo"
